IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bkv-law`
IMPORT `bkv-seat`

-- Tests for the BKV § 9(5) / IFG encoding. Expected values are written from the deposited text (BKV § 9(5), IFG § 1(1) and § 3 no. 4, the gazette), not from this encoding's output.
-- Arguments to `the request that`, in order: federal request, prepared outside the Council and the Ministry, submitted to the Council for its deliberations,
-- a recommendation or report of the Council, another ground for refusing access applies, another statutory confidentiality duty attaches.
-- N is `as in force from 1 August 2026`; O is `as before the 2026 amendment`.

§ `The article's journalist: an external statement submitted to the Council`

-- Under § 9(5) as in force from 1 August 2026, the Council's "Beratungsunterlagen" are confidential, with no limit to those made inside: the external statement is confidential, and § 3 no. 4 IFG bars access.
#ASSERT `section 9(5) BKV makes the document confidential under the reading` `as in force from 1 August 2026` (`the request that` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the requester is entitled to access under the reading` `as in force from 1 August 2026` (`the request that` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- Under the earlier wording only the "intern erstellten Beratungsunterlagen" were covered: the external statement is not confidential and the claim stands.
#ASSERT NOT (`section 9(5) BKV makes the document confidential under the reading` `as before the 2026 amendment` (`the request that` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the requester is entitled to access under the reading` `as before the 2026 amendment` (`the request that` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `A paper made inside the Council or the Ministry`

-- Confidential under both wordings.
#ASSERT `section 9(5) BKV makes the document confidential under the reading` `as in force from 1 August 2026` (`the request that` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `section 9(5) BKV makes the document confidential under the reading` `as before the 2026 amendment` (`the request that` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the requester is entitled to access under the reading` `as before the 2026 amendment` (`the request that` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§ `The documents sentence 1 makes public, and papers not before the Council`

-- A recommendation, an opinion or a closing report is excepted by "mit Ausnahme der in Satz 1 genannten Dokumente", under both wordings.
#ASSERT NOT (`section 9(5) BKV makes the document confidential under the reading` `as in force from 1 August 2026` (`the request that` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the requester is entitled to access under the reading` `as in force from 1 August 2026` (`the request that` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A paper that was never submitted to the Council for its deliberations is not a "Beratungsunterlage".
#ASSERT NOT (`section 9(5) BKV makes the document confidential under the reading` `as in force from 1 August 2026` (`the request that` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§ `IFG § 1(1) and § 3 no. 4: other reasons the claim can fail`

-- Another ground for refusal (the article's footnote 8 assumes none) defeats the claim whatever § 9(5) says.
#ASSERT NOT (`the requester is entitled to access under the reading` `as before the 2026 amendment` (`the request that` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- Another statutory confidentiality duty is a "Rechtsvorschrift" within § 3 no. 4 even where § 9(5) does not reach the paper (the article's third follow-up, which it calls highly unlikely to succeed; encoded as an input).
#ASSERT NOT (`the requester is entitled to access under the reading` `as before the 2026 amendment` (`the request that` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
-- The claim is only against federal authorities (§ 1(1) sentence 1).
#ASSERT NOT (`the requester is entitled to access under the reading` `as before the 2026 amendment` (`the request that` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§ `Grundgesetz Art. 80(1) sentence 3: the Seventh Amending Regulation does not cite § 9(1a) sentence 4`

-- The fact this encoding adds to the record: the gazette preamble cites § 9(1) sentences 1 and 2 only.
#ASSERT NOT (`does the 2026 preamble cite the power for the confidentiality rule`)
#ASSERT count `the powers cited in the preamble of the Seventh Amending Regulation` EQUALS 1
-- The original 1997 preamble does not cite it either (bkv-eingangsformel.txt line 2: § 9 Abs. 1 und 6 and § 193 Abs. 8).
#ASSERT NOT (`the preamble cites the power` `the power needed to make the confidentiality rule` `the powers cited in the original preamble of the BKV`)
-- Controls: a list that does contain the power tests as cited, and a cited power that is not the one needed does not stand in for it.
#ASSERT `the preamble cites the power` `SGB VII 9(1a) sentence 4` (LIST `SGB VII 9(1) sentences 1 and 2`, `SGB VII 9(1a) sentence 4`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the preamble cites the power` `SGB VII 9(1a) sentence 4` (LIST `SGB VII 9(1)`))
#ASSERT `the 2026 amendment of section 9(5) BKV is void for want of citation` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the 2026 amendment of section 9(5) BKV is void for want of citation` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the reading of section 9(5) BKV to apply` FALSE EQUALS `as before the 2026 amendment`
#ASSERT `the reading of section 9(5) BKV to apply` TRUE EQUALS `as in force from 1 August 2026`
